# Compiled blocks are BUILD OUTPUT — untracked, regenerable from the spec.
# Receipts are the tracked half in a real project (they are what the gate reads and
# what proves a pasted block came from the compiler); here, in the package's own
# example, both are untracked because they carry machine-local HMACs and absolute
# paths that mean nothing on another machine.
#
# Keep this directory in git so the gate has somewhere to look on a fresh clone: a
# missing out/ reads as "no receipts", which is the right answer for the wrong reason.
*
!.gitignore
